Calc: a formula naming what Calc lacks keeps the file's result

- XLSX and ODS import mark a formula cell holding an unknown name
  (ocBad) and a loaded result: its result stands, through the hard
  recalc on load too, so its dependents use it and a save writes it
  back (Ely #D-02; PRD §288). Numbers (whole text only), booleans,
  strings including empty ones, and arrays whose every element is
  there. A changed input (Notify) or SetDirty (an edit, a reference
  update) ends that; it then recalcs to #NAME?. The every-change
  broadcast ends it only once loading is done: volatile cells hear
  the load too.
- The mark survives placing a cell, an undo of a reference update and
  a copied sheet; the clipboard drops it.
- ODS writes a kept empty string result, and reads it back.
- An unknown function keeps its spelling instead of being lowercased,
  so the formula written back names it as read.
- .uno:KeptResults lists such cells with their sheet.

